","areaId":"rishikesh","name":"Chaurasi Kutia","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":30.1147,"lng":78.3142},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"rishikesh_wv_chaurasi_kutia","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["chaurasikutia","rishikesh"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"}]},"summary":"Historic ashram where The Beatles stayed and composed music in 1968. Now maintained by the Forest Department, featuring graffiti art in the former meditation caves and cathedral-like lecture hall.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Rishikesh"},{"id":"rishikesh_wv_gita_bhavan","areaId":"rishikesh","name":"Gita Bhavan","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":30.12061,"lng":78.31354},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"rishikesh_wv_gita_bhavan","tickets":[],"signals":{"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["gitabhavan","rishikesh"],"summary":"Place of Guru Shri Ram Sukh Daasji (the great thinker of his time) and popular among the Hindu Brahmin community. Twice a year people gather at this ashram to read the Ramayana together.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Rishikesh","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/India_-_Rishikesh_-_022_-_sunset_over_the_Ganga_%282091421140%29.jpg/1280px-India_-_Rishikesh_-_022_-_sunset_over_the_Ganga_%282091421140%29.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/India_-_Rishikesh_-_022_-_sunset_over_the_Ganga_%282091421140%29.jpg/500px-India_-_Rishikesh_-_022_-_sunset_over_the_Ganga_%282091421140%29.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"McKay Savage from London, UK","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/